  "level": 3,
  "question": {
    "text": "If $z$ is a complex number such that $z^{2}=(\\bar{z})^{2}$, then",
    "image": null
  },
  "options": [
    {
      "id": "szIJ0",
      "text": "$z$ is purely real",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "XPedj",
      "text": "$z$ is purely imaginary",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "TjB3N",
      "text": "either $z$ is purely real or purely imaginary",
      "isCorrect": true,
      "image": null
    },
    {
      "id": "yLfpy",
      "text": "None of these",
      "isCorrect": false,
      "image": null
    }
  ],
  "correctValue": null,
  "solution": {
    "text": "Let $z=x+i y$, then its conjugate $\\bar{z}=x-i y$\r\n\r\nGiven that $z^{2}=(\\bar{z})^{2}$\r\n\r\n$\\begin{array}{l}\r\n\r\n\\Rightarrow x^{2}-y^{2}+2 i x y=x^{2}-y^{2}-2 i x y \\\\\r\n\r\n\\Rightarrow 4 i x y=0\r\n\r\n\\end{array}$",
    "image": null
  },
